r Conferences in September】\nL156: \nL157: February 23, 2026\nL158: ### 【20†QurAlis Demonstrates Effects on Disease Progression and Target Engagement in ANQUR Clinical Trial of QRL-201, a First-in-Class Precision Medicine in Development for Sporadic ALS】\nL159: \nL160: December 29, 2025\nL161: \nL162: ### 【21†QurAlis Confirms Signal of Target Engagement in ALS Patients in Phase 1 Clinical Trial of QRL-101, a Potentially Best-in-Class Selective Kv7.2/7.3 Ion Channel Opener】\nL163: \nL164: December 18, 2025\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAkt Activation With IPL344 Treatment for Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis: First in Human, Open‐Label Study (https://immunitypharma.com/images/publications/muscle_and_nerve_-_2025_-_gotkine_-_akt_activation_with_ipl344_treatment_for_amyotrophic_lateral_sclerosis_first_in_human_1.pdf)\nciteturn291view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 11; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://immunitypharma.com/images/publications/muscle_and_nerve_-_2025_-_gotkine_-_akt_activation_with_ipl344_treatment_for_amyotrophic_lateral_sclerosis_first_in_human_1.pdf\",\"pattern\":\"2017\"}); Total lines: 701\nL72@P1: Harmonization Good Clinical Practice Guidelines. Site medical\nL73@P1: staff were trained and certified in outcomes assessment by the\nL74@P1: Barrow Neurological Institute Clinical Research Organization\nL75@P1: (BNI CRO). Both phases of the study were registered at Clini\nL76@P1: calTrials.gov (28-day dose escalation phase: NCT03652805; ex\u0002tension phase: NCT03755167). Data from an early additional\nL77@P1: participant treated under a similarly designed compassionate\nL78@P1: use protocol (December 2014 to January 2017) are also included.\nL598@P9: grant research support from UCB, Biohaven, Clene Nanomedicine,\nL599@P9: Prilenia, Seelos, Calico, Denali, ALSA, MDA, ALS Finding a Cure,\nL600@P9: ALS One and NINDS.\nL601@P9: Data Availability State